      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: estimate DeepSeek spend when API reports zero cost",
        "body": "Closes #97047\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users running DeepSeek V4 models would see Control UI Spend stay at zero when the DeepSeek API recorded nonzero token usage but returned `usage.cost.total: 0`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWhen transcript scanning sees nonzero token usage, a recorded zero provider total, and known positive model pricing, OpenClaw now recomputes the session cost from pricing instead of treating the provider total as authoritative. The durable usage-cost cache version is bumped so previously cached zero-spend summaries are rebuilt under the corrected semantics.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDeepSeek V4 usage with known pricing now contributes to session and Control UI spend totals instead of appearing as confident zero-cost activity. Unknown/all-zero pricing still surfaces as missing cost rather than guessing spend.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/session-cost-usage.test.ts -- --reporter=dot` — 59 passed\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check src/infra/session-cost-usage.ts src/infra/session-cost-usage.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main --codex-bin .artifacts/codex-flex` — clean, patch correct (0.84)\n",
        "branch": "codex/fix-deepseek-zero-spend",
